    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d265">

                <pb facs="0332" n="216" xml:id="pg216"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 839.00/1085.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Minister Sullivan to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Santo Domingo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-03-07T12:00:00-04:40">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 7, 1914, 12 noon</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>If money for back salaries is not forthcoming at once Provisional Government will
                    go under. If you delay, our hold on the situation will be lost. Prompt relief
                    means keeping all our ground we have gained.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sullivan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
